                            <div class="corner-dot is-tr"></div>
                            <div class="corner-dot is-bl"></div>
                            <div class="corner-dot is-br"></div>
                          </div>
                        </div><button type="button" class="faq-question"><span class="faq-question-text">How does the model fallback system work?</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="100%" height="100%" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                              <path d="M12 4V20M4 12H20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
                            </svg></span></button>
                        <div class="faq-answer">
                          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                            <p class="faq-answer-text">If a provider slows down or returns an error, Synthora automatically retries the request on the next model in your fallback chain, so your agents keep running without any code changes.</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div data-wf--faq-item--variant="base" class="faq-item">
                        <div class="faq-item-bg">
                          <div class="corner-dots">
                            <div class="corner-dot is-tl"></div>
                            <div class="corner-dot is-tr"></div>
                            <div class="corner-dot is-bl"></div>
                            <div class="corner-dot is-br"></div>
                          </div>
                        </div><button type="button" class="faq-question"><span class="faq-question-text">Can I switch models without redeploying code?</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="100%" height="100%" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                              <path d="M12 4V20M4 12H20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
                            </svg></span></button>
                        <div class="faq-answer">
                          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                            <p class="faq-answer-text">Yes. Models are configured in the dashboard, not in your code. Change the default model or routing rules and every agent picks up the new setting on its next request.</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
