                            <div class="corner-dot is-tr"></div>
                            <div class="corner-dot is-bl"></div>
                            <div class="corner-dot is-br"></div>
                          </div>
                        </div><button type="button" class="faq-question"><span class="faq-question-text">Will using an SDK add significant latency?</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="100%" height="100%" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                              <path d="M12 4V20M4 12H20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
                            </svg></span></button>
                        <div class="faq-answer">
                          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                            <p class="faq-answer-text">No. The SDK adds only a few milliseconds per call. Requests are routed through edge locations close to your users, and streaming responses start as soon as the model replies.</p>
